  h1#header Aldi Pramudya
  p.st AI, Data Science, SWE, GIS, anything but #[a(href="https://www.w3schools.com/whatis/whatis_frontenddev.asp") #[span.wr doing frontend]].
  p.summary Semester 7 Computer Science student at #[a(href="https://ipb.ac.id" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") IPB University] (#[span.hl GPA 3.69/4.00], a number I'm legally required to mention). I build and deploy end-to-end ML systems, from data preprocessing and model benchmarking through to API development and cloud deployment. #[span.hl BNSP-Certified Data Analyst], graduate of the #[a(href="https://www.dbs.com/foundation" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") DBS Foundation] × #[a(href="https://www.dicoding.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Dicoding] AI Engineering Cohort, and the person behind MoodSense, a mental health monitoring app that reads your mood better than most people do.
  p.summary I led backend development for #[a(href="https://ittoday.web.id/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") IT-Today 2025] (#[span.hl 2,000+ users], none of whom ever saw my CSS) and design clean-architecture APIs with #[a(href="https://fastapi.tiangolo.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") FastAPI] and #[a(href="https://expressjs.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Express.js]. Comfortable across the stack, from training neural networks in #[a(href="https://www.tensorflow.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") TensorFlow]/#[a(href="https://pytorch.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") PyTorch] to deploying containerized services on #[a(href="https://railway.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Railway] and #[a(href="https://vercel.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Vercel]. And no, the frontend joke above was not a lie. #[span.invisible-text I use LaTex for most of my college assignments. It is way better than MSWord or Google Docs. Also you're not supposed to be able to read this part.]
  blockquote
    span Good design is as little design as possible.
    author Some German guy

  h2#projects Projects?
  h3.project-heading
    | Website for IT-Today 2025
    span.project-date January 2025 – November 2025
  p.project-meta IT-Today 2025
  ul
    li Led a team of #[span.hl 10 developers] across backend, frontend, and UI/UX divisions.
    li Built #[span.hl 20+ RESTful API endpoints] using Express.js, Prisma ORM, and MySQL, with Cloudflare R2 for object storage.
    li Deployed and maintained the API on a cloud platform, serving #[span.hl 2,000+ users] during the event.
    li Conducted code reviews and provided technical support to frontend (React) and UI/UX teams.
    li Gathered and modeled requirements through cross-division collaboration with Executive and Competition committees.
    li This project is still maintained, #[a(href="https://github.com/pusdatin-ittoday/ittod-web-api" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") click here to access github page].

  h3.project-heading
    | Benchmarking Machine Learning Models for SME Success Prediction
    span.project-date May 2026 – June 2026
  p.project-meta INFEST Data Science Competition 2026 (Finalist)
  ul
    li #[a(href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WfvWF3xqLjho3MLbcnwu13Pvby_XCNju/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Click here to access paper].

  h3.project-heading
    | Schola Backend
    span.project-date May 2026 – June 2026
  p.project-meta Academic Project
  ul
    li Architected a Clean Architecture backend with #[span.hl 9 vertical feature slices] (auth, submissions, verification, notifications, dashboard, etc.) using FastAPI and async SQLAlchemy.
    li Designed a verifier approval pipeline with sequential/parallel workflows and HMAC-SHA256 e-signature generation for official document signing.
    li Implemented role-based access control with #[span.hl 4 user roles] (Mahasiswa, Dosen, Pejabat, Operator), JWT authentication, and rate limiting.
    li Built a dynamic form template system with JSON Schema-based field definitions, supporting multiple letter types (SKA, SKPI, etc.) with auto-generated submission IDs.
    li Integrated Cloudflare R2 for file storage, SMTP-based email notifications, and Docker containerization with auto-seeding demo data on first boot.
    li #[a(href="https://github.com/walidan-nadilaw/Schola/tree/main/backend" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Click here to access github page].

  h3.project-heading
    | MoodSense – Student Mental Health Monitor
    span.project-date April 2026 – July 2026
  p.project-meta Coding Camp 2026 – AI Engineer Track, Dicoding × DBS Foundation
  ul
    li Built and deployed the complete backend (Express.js + Prisma ORM + PostgreSQL) and ML API (FastAPI) for a mental health monitoring web app as part of a #[span.hl 6-person Agile/Scrum team].
    li Orchestrated a dual-model inference pipeline combining a BiLSTM-MHSA text sentiment model and an XGBoost/RF survey-based mood classifier, with late fusion to produce a unified mood index.
    li Integrated LLM-powered insights (Gemini/DeepSeek) to generate personalized well-being recommendations, stress/happiness factor analysis, and #[span.hl 5-day mood forecasting] from user check-in history.
    li Designed the PostgreSQL schema (users, mood_logs, mood_predictions, todos, settings, forecasts) and implemented JWT auth, role-based access, and RESTful APIs across #[span.hl 3 feature modules].
    li Deployed #[span.hl all three tiers] to production: Express.js backend and ML API on Railway, React frontend on Vercel, fulfilling all MVP requirements plus mood forecasting and user settings.
    li #[a(href="https://github.com/steezydi/moodsense" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Click here to access github page].
  h3.project-heading
    | KAI Access Sentiment Analysis & Review Scraping
    span.project-date April 2026
  p.project-meta Certification Project
  ul
    li Scraped and processed #[span.hl 20,000 Google Play reviews] from the KAI Access app, then cleaned Indonesian text with slang normalization, stopword removal, and stemming using PySastrawi and NLTK.
    li Built a #[span.hl 3-class sentiment classification] pipeline with rating-based and lexicon-assisted labeling for positive, neutral, and negative feedback.
    li Benchmarked multiple models, including LinearSVC + TF-IDF (86.94% test accuracy on 80/20 split, 87.25% on 70/30 split), tuned TF-IDF + SVM (87.46%), BiLSTM (87.69%), and #[span.hl IndoBERT (87.84%)].
    li Designed a TensorFlow/Keras BiLSTM network with Embedding(20,000, 256), SpatialDropout1D, 2 Bidirectional LSTM layers, dense layers, dropout regularization, class weighting, and early stopping.
    li Used Hugging Face Transformers to fine-tune IndoBERT as the highest-performing baseline, while BiLSTM provided a strong balance between accuracy and efficiency.
  h3.project-heading
    | Soil Moisture Estimation using ANN from Scratch
    span.project-date December 2025
  p.project-meta Academic Project – Artificial Intelligence Course, IPB University
  ul
    li Documented architecture, methodology, and experimental results in an IEEE-format technical report.
    li Awarded a project score of #[span.hl 91.14/100].
    li #[a(href="https://ipb.link/final-ai-report-ann" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer") Click here to access paper].
  h2#experience Experience
  h3.project-heading
    | GIS Analyst and Cartographer
    span.project-date August 2026
  p.project-meta KKN-T Desa Pamijahan
  ul
    li Converted #[span.hl 32 CAD layers] of the latest village boundary data (unreadable by QGIS) into GIS-ready formats.
    li Produced #[span.hl 7 shapefiles] covering administrative boundaries (RT, RW, dusun), rivers, roads, public facility points, and neighboring village boundaries.
    li Repaired #[span.hl 20 invalid polygons] so no weird polygons made it into the final map.
    li Designed and stylized the final map with clean cartographic conventions.
    li Classified #[span.hl 3 land-use classes] (settlements, rice fields, and bare ground) from Google satellite imagery using #[span.hl Meta's Segment Anything Model (SAM)] via TerraLab's #[span.hl AI Segmentation], converting the resulting masks directly into the land-use shapefile.
    li Calculated the total village area (#[span.hl 44,441,121 m² / 4,444.11 ha]) and per-RT area across #[span.hl 32 RT, 9 RW, and 4 dusun] for administrative planning.
    li Received direct appreciation from the village secretary and other aparat desa for the deliverables.
